<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Punic War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">149–146 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Punic War was the last conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, fought from 149 to 146 BCE. After a long siege, Roman forces captured and destroyed Carthage in 146 BCE, and its territory became the Roman province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a> treat the war as the final destruction of the Carthaginian state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/third-punic-war.jpg" alt="Third Punic War" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harrias · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:City_of_Carthage_circa_149_BC.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
